y.github.io/2024_eclipse_webcams/replyv-mdev 6 minutes ago | parent | next [–] Some of the webcams doesn't work, for example in Torreblanca, Castellón. I guess it's normalreplyaljgz 39 minutes ago | prev | next [–] Living in Vancouver, I traveled to Toronto to watch the Eclipse in 2024. We faced a nasty cloud, and had to drive hundreds of kilometers (hundreds of miles) to get a reasonably good view. On the drive back I decided that I'll travel for the one that's happening today, and here I am, in Sierra, with some cool people.Solar eclipses happen rarely enough, and frequently enough, to act as milestones in my life: I can review what happened since the previous one, and make a plan for the next one.They are some of the most magnificent natural phenomena, much more interesting than what's expected.The only other one that I got to see in perfect conditions was in my home town, Isfahan in 1999. I hope this one is perfectly clear again, and I have some resolutions for the next one.replyLongwelwind 10 minutes ago | prev | next [–] Does anyone know if there will be any live feed of the earth viewed from space during the eclipse?replyembedding-shape 1 hour ago | prev | next [–] This is great, can easily see what spots are overfilled with people or not :) I'm still thinking about where exactly I'll go to see it, was thinking Calafell or Vilanova as they're nearby and easily accessible, but probably half of Barcelona thinks the same so better to go a bit inland. Probably I'll end up just outside Lleida I think.Any more Spanish HNers (or temporary visitors) who are going to any specific places to see it? :)replyAl-Khwarizmi 41 minutes ago | parent | next [–] I'm from A Coruña so I should be able to just go down to the street, walk like 100 m and see it. I just hope clouds don't spoil the show (at the moment it's looking good, but here you never know).replyegesko 30 minutes ago | parent | prev | next [–] I'm in Valencia, planning to watch it from the beach.replyiancuandrei 55 minutes ago | parent | prev | next [–] I'll go somewhere around Bilbaoreplydavidricodias 1 hour ago | parent | prev | next [–] Colmenar Viejo seems a great spot ;)replyembedding-shape 1 hour ago | root | parent | next [–] Only 7 hours away :D I'm in the Maresme area, so probably will end up between València and Tarragona on some mountain :) Thanks for the tip though, I'll forward it to my Madrid friends.replyhagen8 59 minutes ago | parent | prev | next [–] Mountains close to leon?replygillesjacobs 15 minutes ago | prev | next [–] Cool, there is no check on the direction of the camera. Various camera's I checked do not seem to point in the direction of the sun during totality. It does filter candidate cameras down though.replyrythmshifter 9 minutes ago | prev | next [–] I get \"access blocked, referer is required\" errors tiled all over the screenreplyfxn 11 minutes ago | prev | next [–] On a Virgin cruise near Ibiza, getting ready for it before sunset. Anyone else in the cruise say hello!replydolmen 9 minutes ago | prev | next [–] Don't bother looking at Iceland: weather is awful right now.replyLawrenceKerr 49 minutes ago | prev | next [–] Doesn't seem like the best of weather now in Iceland, hopefully it clears up. Otherwise it would suck for the people who have planned the trip months if not years in advance only to get a clouded sky, but that's always the risk with astrotravel.replybenoliver999 46 minutes ago | parent | next [–] Surely the smart money is to go to Spainreplyembedding-shape 42 minutes ago | root | parent | next [–] We do get cloudy days too sometimes :) Although today it is looking fairly sunny all over the place: https://i.imgur.com/4LK7xo8.pngreplyTornhoof 58 minutes ago | prev | next [–] Sierra de Guadarrama - Puerto de Cotos https://www.infonieve.es/espacio-nordico/puerto-de-cotos/web... looks decent, different views, good weather.replyNKosmatos 41 minutes ago | prev | next [–] Thanks for posting this, most of us won’t be able to view the eclipse but having a few webcams really helps to get the feeling!Hoping to be able to see the great eclipse of 2027 live ;-)https://www.timeanddate.com/eclipse/solar/2027-august-2replyrythmshifter 10 minutes ago | prev | next [–] I get access blocked errors all over the screenreplyxanthine 1 hour ago | prev | next [–] Sorry for my ignorance, but can someone please explain what I'm looking at here?replymsdz 1 hour ago | parent | next [–] About five hours from now, the sections of Europe indicated on the map will experience a total solar eclipse, with other regions of the continent experiencing a partial one.The map shows feeds to watch it.replyembedding-shape 1 hour ago | parent | prev | next [–] Today there is a eclipse, the map shows where the eclipse will be. In the path of the eclipse, there are also a ton of live webcams, and this map shows those and let you preview the webcams. Does it make sense now?replyrob74 50 minutes ago | root | parent | next [–] Even more specifically, it will start off over Greenland, continue over western Iceland and then finish with the sunset in northeastern Spain and the Balearic Islands.replyvoidUpdate 42 minutes ago | root | parent | next [–] If you pan to the right, it shows that it actually starts in a bit of russiareplydorienh 12 minutes ago | prev | next [–] Sad to be in Singapore where eclipse is not visible!replymatsemann 52 minutes ago | prev | next [–] https://www.timeanddate.com/eclipse/solar/2026-august-12Nice page showing where it will be, with times and visualizations for any point/city.replyhno8a34nwn 19 minutes ago | prev | next [–] Was just dealing with this yesterdayreply4gotunameagain 1 hour ago | prev | next [–] Really cool. I'm quite curious as to where the webcam data came from, as it seems to be from various websites/sources.replyv-mdev 2 minutes ago | parent | next [–] I'm curious tooreplychristkv 17 minutes ago | prev | next [–] We are going to get the full solar eclipse, but to be honest I'm going to enjoy the 