ng Calafell or Vilanova as they're nearby and easily accessible, but probably half of Barcelona thinks the same so better to go a bit inland. Probably I'll end up just outside Lleida I think.Any more Spanish HNers (or temporary visitors) who are going to any specific places to see it? :)replyAl-Khwarizmi 41 minutes ago | parent | next [–] I'm from A Coruña so I should be able to just go down to the street, walk like 100 m and see it. I just hope clouds don't spoil the show (at the moment it's looking good, but here you never know).replyegesko 30 minutes ago | parent | prev | next [–] I'm in Valencia, planning to watch it from the beach.replyiancuandrei 55 minutes ago | parent | prev | next [–] I'll go somewhere around Bilbaoreplydavidricodias 1 hour ago | parent | prev | next [–] Colmenar Viejo seems a great spot ;)replyembedding-shape 1 hour ago | root | parent | next [–] Only 7 hours away :D I'm in the Maresme area, so probably will end up between València and Tarragona on some mountain :) Thanks for the tip though, I'll forward it to my Madrid friends.replyhagen8 59 minutes ago | parent | prev | next [–] Mountains close to leon?replygillesjacobs 15 minutes ago | prev | next [–] Cool, there is no check on the direction of the camera. Various camera's I checked do not seem to point in the direction of the sun during totality. It does filter candidate cameras down though.replyrythmshifter 9 minutes ago | prev | next [–] I get \"access blocked, referer is required\" errors tiled all over the screenreplyfxn 11 minutes ago | prev | next [–] On a Virgin cruise near Ibiza, getting ready for it before sunset. Anyone else in the cruise say hello!replydolmen 9 minutes ago | prev | next [–] Don't bother looking at Iceland: weather is awful right now.replyLawrenceKerr 49 minutes ago | prev | next [–] Doesn't seem like the best of weather now in Iceland, hopefully it clears up. Otherwise it would suck for the people who have planned the trip months if not years in advance only to get a clouded sky, but that's always the risk with astrotravel.replybenoliver999 46 minutes ago | parent | next [–] Surely the smart money is to go to Spainreplyembedding-shape 42 minutes ago | root | parent | next [–] We do get cloudy days too sometimes :) Although today it is looking fairly sunny all over the place: https://i.imgur.com/4LK7xo8.pngreplyTornhoof 58 minutes ago | prev | next [–] Sierra de Guadarrama - Puerto de Cotos https://www.infonieve.es/espacio-nordico/puerto-de-cotos/web... looks decent, different views, good weather.replyNKosmatos 41 minutes ago | prev | next [–] Thanks for posting this, most of us won’t be able to view the eclipse but having a few webcams really helps to get the feeling!Hoping to be able to see the great eclipse of 2027 live ;-)https://www.timeanddate.com/eclipse/solar/2027-august-2replyrythmshifter 10 minutes ago | prev | next [–] I get access blocked errors all over the screenreplyxanthine 1 hour ago | prev | next [–] Sorry for my ignorance, but can someone please explain what I'm looking at here?replymsdz 1 hour ago | parent | next [–] About five hours from now, the sections of Europe indicated on the map will experience a total solar eclipse, with other regions of the continent experiencing a partial one.The map shows feeds to watch it.replyembedding-shape 1 hour ago | parent | prev | next [–] Today there is a eclipse, the map shows where the eclipse will be. In the path of the eclipse, there are also a ton of live webcams, and this map shows those and let you preview the webcams. Does it make sense now?replyrob74 50 minutes ago | root | parent | next [–] Even more specifically, it will start off over Greenland, continue over western Iceland and then finish with the sunset in northeastern Spain and the Balearic Islands.replyvoidUpdate 42 minutes ago | root | parent | next [–] If you pan to the right, it shows that it actually starts in a bit of russiareplydorienh 12 minutes ago | prev | next [–] Sad to be in Singapore where eclipse is not visible!replymatsemann 52 minutes ago | prev | next [–] https://www.timeanddate.com/eclipse/solar/2026-august-12Nice page showing where it will be, with times and visualizations for any point/city.replyhno8a34nwn 19 minutes ago | prev | next [–] Was just dealing with this yesterdayreply4gotunameagain 1 hour ago | prev | next [–] Really cool. I'm quite curious as to where the webcam data came from, as it seems to be from various websites/sources.replyv-mdev 2 minutes ago | parent | next [–] I'm curious tooreplychristkv 17 minutes ago | prev | next [–] We are going to get the full solar eclipse, but to be honest I'm going to enjoy the transitions more than the actual eclipse itself. It's not like the glasses will give you a great view of the actual sun itself compared to a live professional camera setup so I'll be having the tv on to se the \"filtered\" view of the sun directly instead of trying to stare at it. I'll peak a glance once in awhile.replylifestyleguru 22 minutes ago | prev | next [–] I'm declaring that sun will die a over northern Spain and western Iceland by the end of the day.replyrimworld 17 minutes ago | prev | next [–] cool -thxreplyMadrasTh0rn 46 minutes ago | prev | next [–] Very coolreplymoron4hire 56 minutes ago | prev [–] I took my kids out of school and took an unplanned day off work in the middle of an important meeting series to drive 5 hours west from Virginia to Ohio to see the last eclipse. The schools and my boss were both yelling at me, both saying the eclipse wasn't a good enough excuse. I'm sorry, but it definitely was. I am so glad I did that. I would do it again in a heartbeat.replyUncle_Brumpus 36 minutes ago | parent | next [–] I drove ~3 hours to the Vermont-Canada border... and then drove 14 hours home. I'd also do it again in a heartbeat.I almost signed up for a live-work program for a big\n=== END PAGE TEXT ===\n\nGoal: Survey the top 3 Hacker News stories:\n\n1. From the front page, identify the FIRST 3 st